 </Files>
 
+# [F2-06] Pages that put ONE PERSON'S data on screen (the checkout form, the account, an invoice, an order's status, the payment
+# result, a review invite, the admin) must not come back from the browser's back/forward cache. "no-cache" above still
+# allows it; measured in Chromium: after Back, the typed checkout form (name, phone), the invoice (name, address) and the
+# signed-in account (name, email) were restored from memory with no request at all, for whoever held the device by then.
+# "no-store" makes Back ask the server again, so what is shown follows the session as it is NOW. The shell is a few kB
+# and only these routes pay for it; every other page keeps the 304 above. THE_REQUEST is the line the browser sent,
+# before the rewrite to seo-page.php (REQUEST_URI would already be /api/seo-page.php).
+<Files "seo-page.php">
+  Header set Cache-Control "no-store" "expr=(%{REQUEST_STATUS} == 200 || %{REQUEST_STATUS} == 304) && %{THE_REQUEST} =~ m!^[A-Z]+ /(checkout|account|invoice|payment/result|track|review|backends)([/? ]|$)!"
+</Files>
+
 # Hero slides and brand logos are IMAGES served by api.php, each URL carrying
